<title>FINLAND: HACKMAN PUSHING FOR NORDIC ALLIANCE - PAPER.</title>
<headline>HACKMAN PUSHING FOR NORDIC ALLIANCE - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish consumer goods maker Oy Hackman Ab has been driving talks on a consumer goods alliance with Swedish Orrefors and Danish Royal Copenhagen, daily Kauppalehti reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It quoted outgoing CEO Curt Lindbom as saying that there are no talks at the moment but that they should continue.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been in the drivers' seat here. From our initiative there have been talks with Danish Royal Copenhagen and Swedish Orrefors,&quot; it quoted Lindbom as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;A Nordic alliance would be a natural solution. We are still small by ourselves,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
